WEBVTT

1
00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:07.589
Your skin is your own. So is your hair.

2
00:00:10.800 --> 00:00:14.051
So why should your treatment be one setting, for everyone?

3
00:00:15.900 --> 00:00:21.369
Introducing advanced four-wavelength diode laser hair reduction, at Belle Afrique.

4
00:00:21.900 --> 00:00:23.359
Here’s how it works.

5
00:00:23.600 --> 00:00:28.707
Laser light passes through the skin, and is drawn to the dark pigment in the hair root.

6
00:00:28.900 --> 00:00:35.479
The root is heated, and weakened. So over a course of sessions, hair grows back slower, finer, and less.

7
00:00:36.300 --> 00:00:41.940
But hair sits at different depths, and every skin tone is different. So we use four wavelengths.

8
00:00:42.200 --> 00:00:45.536
755, for fine hair near the surface.

9
00:00:45.600 --> 00:00:47.528
808, the all-rounder.

10
00:00:47.700 --> 00:00:49.820
940, reaching deeper.

11
00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:54.381
And 1064, the deepest, important for darker skin tones.

12
00:00:56.800 --> 00:00:59.517
True diode laser. Not IPL.

13
00:01:00.020 --> 00:01:02.400
Lee Billy Chisale: We don’t treat everybody with the same setting.

14
00:01:02.760 --> 00:01:07.150
We assess, we test, and we design the treatment around your skin.

15
00:01:08.500 --> 00:01:13.201
Every new client begins with a professional consultation, and a patch test.

16
00:01:14.500 --> 00:01:19.201
Over a course of sessions: fewer hairs, slower regrowth, and smoother skin.

17
00:01:19.400 --> 00:01:22.821
For him, too: fewer shaving bumps, and ingrown hairs.

18
00:01:28.300 --> 00:01:32.681
Belle Afrique. Four wavelengths. One individual treatment plan.

19
00:01:33.100 --> 00:01:35.903
Book your private laser consultation today.
